### III. PHP SUB-MODULE ARCHITECTURE & FILE BREAKDOWN

Monolithic PHP files must be systematically broken down into distinct sub-modules housed within `includes/[module_name]/`. Each sub-module file must maintain complete isolation:

1. `class-sywat-[module].php` (Controller Shell & Entry Point):
   - Handles sub-module inclusions (`require_once`), shortcodes (`add_shortcode`), capability/permission checks (`sywat_can_access_*`), and execution orchestration.

2. MANDATORY DATA & HELPER FILE SEPARATION:
   - `[module]-data.php` (Data Access & Metric Engines): Pure database queries (`WP_User_Query`, `$wpdb` calls), user meta getters, raw dataset aggregations, and statistical calculation engines. Must NEVER render HTML or format presentation strings.
   - `[module]-helpers.php` (Formatting & Presentation Helpers): Pure scalar/array payload formatters, HTML/badge label generators, array sorting weight maps, and DOB/age division calculators. Must NEVER execute database queries or fetch meta directly.

3. `[module]-actions.php`:
   - Pure POST request processing, nonce verification, data sanitization, AJAX endpoint hooks, and database mutations. Returns standardized alert markup (`$action_notice`) or JSON responses.

4. `[module]-views.php` & `[module]-modals.php`:
   - `[module]-views.php`: Visual HTML renderers for primary UI structures (tabs, master cards, filter bars, tables).
   - `[module]-modals.php`: Pop-up overlay templates. Must receive pre-calculated data payload arrays and format output via helpers.

5. BOARD POSITIONS & AUTOMATED ROLE SYNCHRONIZATION POLICY:
   - Board Position assignments saved under Board Management (`save_board_member`) serve as the single source of truth for Officer and Governor roles (`tfaa_president`, `tfaa_field_governor`, etc.).
   - Board position saves MUST automatically add matching WP user roles and revoke unassigned officer roles.
   - General profile updates (`update_member`) MUST preserve active board officer roles so profile saves never strip assigned board status.

