### V. STRICT CSS, HTML COMPONENT & UI POLICIES

1. ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION OF INLINE STYLES & EMBEDDED CSS:
   - NEVER put `<style>...</style>` tags inside PHP templates or functions.
   - NEVER use inline `style="..."` attributes on HTML elements in PHP views, forms, or modal templates. Use centralized CSS utility classes (`.sywat-mt-3`, `.sywat-form-grid-2`, `.sywat-hidden`).

2. DESIGN TOKEN & COLOR PALETTE BINDING:
   - Primary action triggers (submits, save buttons, sign-in buttons) MUST map exclusively to SYWAT Action Blue (`#0284c7` background, `#0369a1` hover, `.sywat-btn-primary`).
   - Secondary triggers map to `.sywat-btn-secondary`, destructive triggers map to `.sywat-btn-danger` (`#dc2626`), and confirmation states map to `.sywat-btn-success`.

3. STRICT MODAL CONTROL COMPONENT MANDATE:
   - Modal close buttons (`.sywat-modal-close`) and modal footer action buttons MUST strictly use native `<button type="button">` or `<button type="submit">` elements.
   - NEVER convert modal buttons or close triggers into `<a>` anchor links to workaround JavaScript state handling or URL parameter cleanup bugs. 
   - All URL parameter removal (e.g., clearing `edit_board_user_id`) MUST be executed cleanly via `window.history.replaceState()` inside `assets/js/sywat-members.js`.

4. STRICT SEPARATION OF COSMETIC VS. STRUCTURAL EDITS:
   - Cosmetic, spacing, label positioning, and alignment fixes MUST be executed exclusively within CSS files (`assets/css/`).
   - NEVER modify PHP view files or template wrappers to solve a visual styling bug unless an RCA explicitly proves a missing CSS class or DOM element is required.

5. SINGLE-SELECTOR SCOPE ISOLATION:
   - CSS edits must strictly target the specific component or class requiring adjustment.
   - NEVER alter parent layout wrappers, default container flex behaviors, or global rules when fixing an isolated child element alignment.

